cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research repository, please cite the specific repository version or commit and separately cite the underlying data sources."
title: "Counterterrorism, Ethnosectarian Context & Islamic State Attack Patterns"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lystad"
    given-names: "John S."
repository-code: "https://github.com/LystadJS/counterterrorism_ethnosectarian_islamic_state"
url: "https://github.com/LystadJS/counterterrorism_ethnosectarian_islamic_state"
abstract: >-
  R-based research workflows integrating terrorism event data with Iraqi
  district-level spatial, ethnosectarian, and population information for
  reproducible analysis of Islamic State-linked attack patterns. The
  repository is an active research workspace and should not be treated as a
  frozen publication release unless tied to a tagged version or publication.
keywords:
  - counterterrorism
  - terrorism
  - Islamic State
  - Iraq
  - computational social science
  - spatial analysis
  - reproducible research
